1. Why does a negative dx or dy not make the final distance negative?
Because pow(dx, 2) and pow(dx, 2) are squared, being incapable of yielding a negative answer
2. What mathematical role does sqrt() play after adding the squared differences?
It reverses the square, so that it can be used in units of measurement.
3. How would the result change if pow(dx, 2) were replaced with dx + 2?
It will add it, not multiply it.
